"Initial Zoom","Hold","Toggle","Easing","Ease Out Cubic","Linear","Ease Out Sine","Ease In Out Sine","Ease Out Quad","Ease In Out Quad","Ease In Out Cubic","Ease Out Expo","Ease In Out Expo","Zoom In Time","s","Zoom Out Time","Scroll Zoom","Scroll Steps","Zoom Per Step","%","Sensitivity","Retain Steps","Custom Crosshair","Replaces the vanilla crosshair with a configurable shape and colour, optional black outline, and a dynamic mode that opens up on a target.","#3ce7c4","px","°","FPS HUD","Shows the current frames-per-second counter on the HUD.",
"Top-Left","Keystrokes","Displays your WASD and mouse-button presses as on-screen keys.","#10131a","CPS Display","Counts your clicks-per-second for left and/or right mouse buttons, with a peak (max) readout.","#ffffff","Coordinates","Shows your current XYZ position, facing and biome, with optional Nether↔Overworld coordinate conversion.","WAILA","\"What Am I Looking At\" — a Jade/WTHIT-style panel for the block or entity under your crosshair: icon, name, mob health/armour, crop growth, harvest tool, redstone/note/beehive state and the source mod.",
"Show Entities","Show Health","Show Tool","Show Mod","Chunk Borders","Draws the chunk-aligned grid around you, plus optional slime-chunk boxes and the 512-block region-file boundary.","#44e05a","#8a5cff","Light Overlay","Marks nearby blocks dark enough for hostile mobs to spawn (red = always, yellow = night only). Optional light-level numbers + threshold.","#ff3030","#ffdd33","A searchable, scrollable browser of every item (JEI/REI/EMI-style); press the bound key in-world to open it.","Saturation","AppleSkin: draws food-restoration preview on the hunger bar, a saturation gauge, and a health-restoration preview on the health bar, with the flashing overlay animation. Optional text line too.",
"HUD Overlay","Food Preview","Saturation Bar","Health Preview","MiniHUD","Compact info lines: facing, biome, light, chunk, time, TPS, slime, speed, ping.","#9aa4b6","TPS Display","Shows the measured server tick rate (ticks per second).","Ping Display","Shows your connection latency to the server in milliseconds.","Armor HUD","Shows worn armour (and optionally the held item) as icons with durability bars, a low-durability warning tint, and total armour points.","Inventory HUD","Draws your inventory as an item grid on the HUD — main rows plus optional hotbar and armour columns, hidden while a screen is open.",
"Damage Tint","Flashes a vignette around the screen edges when you take damage, plus a pulsing border when your health is low.","#ff2a2a","Effect Timers","Lists active potion effects (beneficial first), colour-coded by category, with the remaining time and an ambient marker.","Durability","Shows the remaining durability of your held, offhand and worn-armour items, with optional percentage, remaining-% colouring, and low-only filtering.","Reach Display","Shows the distance to the block or entity under your crosshair, optionally entity-only and colour-graded by distance.",
"Auto Sprint","Always sprint without holding the sprint key.","Toggle Sneak","Press the bound key to toggle sneaking on/off instead of holding it; shows an indicator while active.","No Fog","Disables distance fog so the world is visible out to the render edge.","Freecam","Detaches the camera to fly freely with the movement keys while your player stays frozen in place. Press the bound key to toggle.","Shoulder Surfing","Shoulder-Surfing-Reloaded-style third-person camera (press F5): smoothed offset, wall-collision pull-in, aim/sprint state multipliers. Bound key swaps shoulders.",
"Minimap","A north-up top-down minimap of the terrain around you. Heavier than the text HUD lines (a bounded block scan) — opt-in.","mousetweaks","Mouse Tweaks","Hold Shift + left-drag across inventory slots to quick-move each one you touch.","itemscroller","Item Scroller","Scroll the mouse wheel over an inventory slot to move items (Stack mode = whole stack, Single = one item). Ctrl = matching, Alt = whole inventory.","Scroll Mode","Stack","Single","Controlling","Opens a searchable vanilla-keybind editor (rebind, unbind, conflict highlight). Press the bound key in-world.",
